{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794843411,"nonce":"+BqVKUAyME5c/DstlMfxKkdA4T0=","title":"hxnme: the hxn media engine, over hxn-window, hxn-av, hxnsl and hxn-gpu","message":"An engine core for GUI and interactive apps, games, audio and visual systems, natively, on Android and iOS, and in the browser. It gives a program an application loop, input, rendering, audio, addressable assets, entities and UI, and the `hxnme` command scaffolds, runs, hot-reloads and packages the app. Programs can still reach `GpuDevice`, `Window` or an `AudioDecoder` directly.\n\n\n- Package `hxn.me`, one repository hx-n/hxnme with the haxelib and the CLI.\n- The core is Haxe, so Ash hot-reloads engine and game code alike. Work that has to be native or fast goes into hxn libraries (mixer, text shaping, layout, accessibility) under hxn's usual rules.\n- No default release runtime: `hxnme.toml` names the runtime for each target (hxcpp, HashLink, Ash JIT or AOT). Development runs on Ash for hot reload.\n- The foundation gaps (M0) are filled as separate hxn libraries before engine code starts.\n\n\n1. App: entry, fixed-step update and variable render, frame pacing on the surface's vsync, lifecycle (suspend and resume on mobile, page visibility on the web), windows and DPI; `hl.Api.checkReload()` each frame in development.\n2. Input: action maps over keyboard, mouse, touch, gamepad and pointer; text input with IME.\n3. Render: over hxn-gpu. A frame graph of passes and transient targets; a 2D batcher (sprites, shapes, nine-slice, text); cameras, render targets, post-processing; 3D meshes and materials later. Shaders are hxnsl classes, shared by engine and game.\n4. Audio: sound effects, music streamed through hxn-av's decoders, buses, spatial panning, on hxn-audio.\n5. Assets: every asset has an address and labels, with groups and dependencies, in a catalog generated at compile time. Loading is async through `hxn.Future`, unloading reference-counted. Groups bundle for remote delivery (a CDN for the web). A cook step builds per-platform textures, audio, font atlases and shaders. The dev server pushes asset changes into the running program.\n6. Entities: an archetype ECS with component storage and typed queries generated by macros; systems in phases; hierarchy as components; prefabs and scenes as serialized assets.\n7. UI: a retained widget tree driven by `hxn.Reactive` and `Signal`; flex layout (taffy through hxn); theming, text fields, scrolling; accessibility through AccessKit. Usable without the ECS.\n8. Math types, tweens, timers, storage and preferences.\n\n\nRust, reusing hxn-cli's Ash page, mobile and packaging code.\n\n- `hxnme new \u003cname\u003e [--template app|game2d|game3d]`: `hxnme.toml` (id, version, targets and their runtimes, icons, orientation, permissions, signing), `src/`, `assets/`, `shaders/`.\n- `hxnme dev [desktop|web|android|ios]`: a warm Haxe compilation server rebuilds `main.hl` on save; `ash --mode hybrid --hot-reload` runs it; assets are watched and pushed; web pages and mobile devices take reloads from the dev server.\n- `hxnme run`, `hxnme build \u003ctarget\u003e [--release]`.\n- `hxnme package \u003ctarget\u003e`: `.app`/`.dmg`, a Windows installer or zip, AppImage, `.apk`/`.aab`, `.ipa` or an Xcode project, a static web build with COOP/COEP headers.\n\n\n- M0 Foundation: hxn-window in the browser; hxn-audio; hxn-text; file access; mobile runs of window and GPU in CI. Done when a window, a sound and a line of text run on every platform.\n- M1 Core: app loop, input actions, 2D renderer, assets v1, `new`/`run`/`build` for desktop and web. A small 2D game sample runs everywhere.\n- M2 Dev loop: `hxnme dev` with code and asset hot reload; Android and iOS runs.\n- M3 Entities: ECS, scenes, prefabs, serialization, audio integration, tweens.\n- M4 UI: layout, widgets, text input and IME, accessibility. A form-style app sample.\n- M5 3D: frame graph, meshes, materials, post-processing.\n- M6 Delivery: packaging, signing, store and web deploys, docs.\n\nEach milestone gets its own issue when it starts.","files":null}]}